==Strategy==
For what is supposed to be the final boss of the Stories of Legend, the mighty Mecha-Bun is, ironically, disappointingly easy. At first glance, Mecha-Bun seems very threatening, as it has 3 million HP, 37K DPS, an Omni Strike piercing up to 240 range (which is only 10 less than [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]), and a fairly fast 23 speed, this mechanical menace has insane pushing power as well if not kept in check. Fortunately, most of the difficulty is neutralized by stacking [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cats]]. With a range of 300, they can comfortably outrange Mecha-Bun's Omni Strike by 60 and likely Freeze it in its tracks. To make things convenient, the stage also starts off with a Li'l Bun Bun to help stack them up.

While Necro-Dancer Cat is already very strong on their own, their Single Attack may be problematic due to the peons of the stage. Pair them with Sanzo who can act as supplementary CC in case Mecha-Bun gets out of the Freeze chain, and attackers like Cameraman Cat to clear the peons. Once Mecha-Bun is gone, whatever attackers that are brought along can easily destroy the base and claim victory.

